hi joel,

thanks for applying for the android developer intern position =E2=80=94 we'=
d like
to take this a step further.

attached is a take-home assignment. it's built around a practice product we
made up called Tiffin, an app for ordering a daily tiffin from home
kitchens. three Compose screens, one piece of agent-written code to fix,
and a release note.

a few things worth saying up front:

   - it's about four hours of work, and you have 48 hours from this email.
   - it's deliberately more than four hours of ideal work. cutting the
   right scope is part of what we're reading, so an honest cut beats a
   half-finished screen.
   - use ai on it =E2=80=94 Claude, Cursor, Copilot, whatever you work with=
. that's
   how this team writes code, and tasks 2 and 4 are about whether you can
   direct an agent and catch it when it's wrong.
   - if anything in the spec is unclear, just ask. asking a good question
   counts in your favour here.

one attachment: the brief (pdf). send everything back on this same thread =
=E2=80=94
a github link (public, or private with propel-hiring invited), a debug apk,
and a screen recording under 90 seconds.

good luck =E2=80=94 looking forward to installing it.

*regards*,
sourav badami
co-founder, propel <https://gopropel.in>
powering global breakout products! <https://gopropel.in>

